{"requirements":[{"id":"daily_rotation","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule specifies daily rotation, is parsed as rotating after one day, and is included in an enabled, active, persistent daily logrotate timer. A forced rotation also directly demonstrated that the rule operates, and the effective configuration persisted through restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3dee52961d6b4aa4","cmd-33b9142c5de346ab","cmd-a6d857f97edd48c5","cmd-fc6f14f9198b4073"]},{"id":"compressed_retention","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations of /var/log/inventory/app.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The exercised rule reported rotateCount 7, produced a gzip-compressed archive with verified integrity and content, and remained effective after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33b9142c5de346ab","cmd-2dbda5dedf174c63","cmd-a6d857f97edd48c5","cmd-fc6f14f9198b4073"]},{"id":"writer_continuity","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A held-open writer used inode 290760 before and after copy-truncate rotation. Its pre-rotation entry appeared in the archive and its post-rotation entry appeared in the active log, directly demonstrating continuity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e60d7bd3048143eb","cmd-33b9142c5de346ab","cmd-2dbda5dedf174c63"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"One unnecessary, low-risk mutation was identified: the temporary writer command created or truncated /var/tmp/inventory-writer.out, never consulted it, and no captured command removed it; it was therefore not shown reverted, although its final presence is unconfirmed because lifecycle inventory covered /tmp rather than /var/tmp. The configuration change, forced rotation, bounded test writes, restart, and recovery write otherwise had clear task or mandatory evidence roles. Final observations show no failed units, new listening exposure, or package damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e60d7bd3048143eb","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three public task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node1 restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the node became temporarily unavailable, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered with a running system, zero failed units, active scheduler, matching configuration and archive checksums, and a writable log. The fixed boot-identity observations independently agree with the executor sequence.","limitations":["No naturally scheduled rotation over a full day was observed; daily execution is established by the effective parsed rule and active persistent daily timer, while the behavioral rotation test was forced.","Only one archive generation was exercised, so eviction at the eighth rotation was not directly observed; seven-file retention is supported by the effective rotateCount setting.","The final lifecycle snapshot did not inventory /var/tmp, so the final presence of inventory-writer.out cannot be independently confirmed."]}
